{"id": "LAG-03", "summary": "A settings save writes and syncs its files with the store lock free: every disk change goes through an injected step runner that probes the lock with try_lock (free during every file write, held only for the renames), the steps run equal the plan made under the lock, saves take turns, a direct save that lands in between is kept, and a failed step returns its error with the file untouched.", "tests": [{"runner": "cargo", "file": "src-tauri/src/state_lock_board_tests.rs", "name": "state::lock_board_tests::a_settings_write_never_holds_the_store_lock"}, {"runner": "cargo", "file": "src-tauri/src/state_lock_board_tests.rs", "name": "state::lock_board_tests::renames_land_under_the_store_lock_and_saves_take_turns"}, {"runner": "cargo", "file": "src-tauri/src/state_lock_board_tests.rs", "name": "state::lock_board_tests::what_reaches_the_disk_is_the_snapshot_taken_under_the_lock"}, {"runner": "cargo", "file": "src-tauri/src/state_lock_board_tests.rs", "name": "state::lock_board_tests::two_saves_in_a_row_end_with_the_newest_state_on_disk"}, {"runner": "cargo", "file": "src-tauri/src/state_lock_board_tests.rs", "name": "state::lock_board_tests::a_save_that_lands_in_between_is_not_lost"}, {"runner": "cargo", "file": "src-tauri/src/state_lock_board_tests.rs", "name": "state::lock_board_tests::a_failed_write_reports_the_error_and_changes_nothing"}]}
